# 🔴 The WASM binary must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
# On a machine with core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone would rewrite 0x0A bytes inside the binary,
# producing a .wasm that is corrupt but present. The SHA-256 artifact test would catch it, which
# is the point of that test, but it should never get that far.
*.wasm binary

# Keep the readable WASM source and the JS deterministic too, so the committed hash of the binary
# stays reproducible from the source on any platform.
*.wat text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
